  </ol>

  <h2 id="skills">Skills that protect the decision no matter which stream you choose</h2>

  <p>
    Whichever path you choose, a few skills apply universally and specifically help close the gaps the data above shows. Your degree still matters — it opens doors and, in regulated fields like medicine or law, is the door. <strong>What turns it into an actual high-income skill portfolio</strong> is what you build alongside it: the right skill mix for you, proof of work the market can verify, communication that gets you noticed, positioning inside the field, personal fit, and a realistic read on the financial reality of the path.
  </p>

